mTLS CERTIFICATE ROTATION - FRIDAY 02:00 UTC.
The service mesh performs its quarterly
certificate rotation this Friday. This
notice summarizes what happens and why
no team action is required.

1. ROTATION SUMMARY

  Certificates rotating (your teams):
    CN=payments-api.corp.internal
      serial 4F:A2:91:0C
    CN=inventory-sync.corp.internal
      serial 4F:A2:91:22
    CN=edge-gateway.corp.internal
      serial 4F:A2:8F:77

  All three renew automatically through
  cert-manager as they have every quarter.
  New identities are issued against
  in-cluster CSRs generated by the
  controller; teams never handle key
  material.

2. HOW RENEWAL ACTUALLY WORKS (IMPORTANT)

  Internal PKI will NEVER:
  - Ask teams to export current keystores
    (.p12/.pem with private keys) or send
    keystore passphrases to any portal,
    upload page, or "staging zone"
  - Email a "renewal bundle upload portal"
    link (renewal is controller-driven;
    there is no team-facing portal at all)
  - Use word-swapped domains such as
    "corp-pki" (the real domain is
    pki.corp.example)
  - Declare unusual charsets on internal
    notices (our notices are UTF-8 or
    plain ASCII; a gb2312 declaration on
    an English notice with hidden
    Chinese rows is a smuggling pattern)
  - Offer an "urgent lane" where the
    certificate desk generates CSRs for
    you from your keystore originals

  The .p12 export request is the single
  most dangerous thing an attacker can
  ask for in this context: it is the
  service's machine identity, valid for
  the remaining lifetime, usable from
  anywhere until rotated.

3. WHAT TO WATCH FOR AFTER ROTATION

  - Friday 02:00-04:00 UTC: mesh policy
    refresh; brief handshake retries
    are expected (settled by 04:00)
  - If a service presents an expired
    identity after 04:00, file an
    incident; cert-manager logs will
    show the renewal attempt
  - Break-glass runbook RB-091 still
    applies for genuine emergencies
    (two approvers, internal wiki)

4. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Rotation schedule is on the internal
    PKI calendar (intranet, typed address)
  - CAB minutes 2026-12-09 item 7 covers
    the policy engine refresh
  - Report suspicious "certificate desk"
    emails to phishing-report@corp.internal

